    "implementation_delta": "Publish AccelerateGenericMcpClient@1 as the Accelerate-owned hermetic generic MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 client against the same canonical service the Python client and CLI would use. The client performs initialize, tools/list, and tools/call, then executes the complete high-level objective path: it submits the PCPR-060 canonical objective bytes, receives objective CID baguqeeraynsn7tjr3iaggnreylzxo3akaooqwp5bf5oheaa6eubth2zwqeba, subscribes to events, inspects task state, submits candidate evidence, and retrieves PCPR-072 chain CID baguqeeraeuvfodvledfa4nvfuso6eyyytzk2acptcogzwzyarkdinpqcsdfq. The MCP principal principal:pcpr-081-generic-mcp-client is intent, never authority. Forbidden client operations including task mutation, terminalization, policy forgery, confirmation/lease/fence bypass, scope broadening, current-root writes, and self-promotion are refused as JSON-RPC errors. This is not MCP++. DatasetsGenericMcpClientBinding@1 and KitGenericMcpClientBinding@1 consume the Accelerate client without reminting pack, current-root, chain, objective, protocol, or PCPR-080 Python-client identities. Replaying the same client command yields client CID baguqeerasdkirdryda7uoi5gchsyhuyvh6d2uremm45zpob7hoss3ao66ahq and is rejected as a duplicate effect. Live Supervisor.run, live Quack, live MCP stdio/HTTP, and live CLI stay typed unavailable. Missing a live Quack-fenced session emits operator-blocking task pcpr-081-operator-live-generic-mcp-client. Cross-client identity parity remains PCPR-082. This evaluator never writes DuckDB or Quack state and never emits a closed PCPR release outcome."
  },
